❗️ Last night, the Armed Forces of the Russian Federation delivered a massive strike by ground-based high-precision weapons and attack drones at a communication centre in Kiev region, Ukraine's energy system facilities ensuring military production, and the port infrastructure of Izmail.

The following targets were engaged:

📍 in Kiev, the De Novo data processing centre, one of the main Internet exchange points that ensures the processing, storage, and transmission of information in the interests of the AFU;

📍 in Kiev region:

▫️ the Kievskaya electrical substation (the settlement of Nalivaykovka), which ensures the transmission of electricity and its distribution to the defence industry facilities in Kiev and Kiev region;

▫️ the Kievskaya hydropower station (the settlement of Vyshgorod), which supports defence industry facilities in the northern part of Kiev region;

▫️ the Tripolskaya thermal power plant, which provides power to defence industry facilities in the southern part of Kiev region;

▫️ a battery energy storage station in Gorenichi, used for energy accumulation for uninterrupted operation of military facilities in Kiev and Kiev region;

📍 in Odessa region – production and industrial facilities in the port of Ishmael, which provides reception, storage, and transportation of military cargo and fuel for the needs of the AFU.

💥 In addition, a dry cargo ship delivering military materiel and dual-use cargo for the AFU to the port of Odessa was hit in the north-western part of the Black Sea.

🔹Russian Defence Ministry
